     "text": "```python\n# Function to compute the average of the diagonal elements of a matrix\n# This function adheres to the latest coding guidelines provided by Pedro, including:\n# - Variable names start with 'wr_'\n# - Function names end with '_a'\n# - Function arguments start with 'x_'\n# - Use of Doxygen-style comments for documentation\n# - Use of a code linter (e.g., Pylint) to ensure code quality and consistency\n\nwr_avg_diagonal_a = x_matrix_a:\n\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the average of the diagonal elements of a square matrix.\n\n    Parameters:\n    x_matrix_a (list of list of int/float): A square matrix (n x n).\n\n    Returns:\n    float: The average of the diagonal elements.\n\n    Raises:\n    ValueError: If the input is not a square matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Check if the matrix is square\n    n = len(x_matrix_a)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"The matrix must not be empty.\")\n    for row in x_matrix_a:\n        if len(row) != n:\n            raise ValueError(\"The matrix must be square.\")\n\n    # Calculate the sum of diagonal elements\n    diagonal_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        diagonal_sum += x_matrix_a[i][i]\n\n    # Calculate the average\n    return diagonal_sum / n\n```",
